= Parkinson's law =

{{:Parkinson's law/Simple}}

== Origin and meanings ==
'''Parkinson's law''' names a satirical observation introduced by historian C. Northcote Parkinson in ''The Economist'' on 19 November 1955. Its opening aphorism concerns work occupying the time allotted to it. The essay's principal organizational argument concerns administrative staffs growing even where a department's apparent operational workload declines.<ref name="original">Parkinson, C. Northcote. “Parkinson's Law.” ''The Economist'', 19 November 1955. Historical reprint of the essay: https://www.panarchy.org/parkinson/parkinsonlaw.html (1958 version; editorial commentary on that site is not treated as evidence).</ref>

Parkinson proposed two mutually reinforcing mechanisms: administrators prefer adding subordinates over peers who might rival them, and additional officials generate correspondence and coordination work for one another. His deliberately mock-scientific presentation was social criticism, not a validated natural law.<ref name="original"/>

== Interpretation and evidence ==
The aphorism is often applied to deadlines and task scoping. The organizational argument is about incentives, hierarchy, and endogenous administrative work; these are related but '''not identical empirical hypotheses'''. Parkinson selected historical British administrative comparisons rather than conducting a controlled causal study. Administrative growth can also reflect changed duties, regulation, technology, or measurement boundaries.<ref name="breton">Breton, Albert, and Ronald Wintrobe (1979). “Bureaucracy and state intervention: Parkinson's Law?” ''Canadian Public Policy'' 5? Bibliographic details should be checked against publisher record; see publisher DOI landing page: https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1754-7121.1979.tb01813.x</ref>

== Practical use ==
Treat the law as a question to investigate: Is an expanded schedule associated with extra work, or does the task genuinely require more time? Does administrative headcount reflect coordination overhead or additional services? Compare defined outcomes, workload, quality, and organizational functions before attributing change to Parkinson's proposed mechanisms.

== Limits ==
No universal percentage growth rate or deterministic duration formula follows from the essay. Shortening a deadline can reduce checking, safety, or quality; expanding a department can be justified by new obligations. The essay's satirical statistics should not be promoted to general empirical constants.

